<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">First Portuguese Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1910 CE – 1926 CE · capital Lisbon</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Portugal's first republic, an era of anticlerical reform and chronic instability with some 45 governments in under 16 years.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the assassination of King Carlos I in 1908, republican sentiment grew in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a>. On 5 October 1910 a revolt by soldiers, sailors and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carbonaria-portugal">Carbonária</a> militants overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-ii-of-portugal">Manuel II</a>, and a provisional government under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teofilo-braga">Teófilo Braga</a> proclaimed the republic, ending the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Constitution of 1911 created a parliamentary republic. Governments led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-costa">Afonso Costa</a> separated Church and state, expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> and legalised divorce. Portugal entered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> in 1916 and suffered heavy losses at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-la-lys-1918">La Lys</a> in 1918. Strikes, coups, bombings and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidonio-pais">Sidónio Pais's</a> brief dictatorship of 1917-1918 marked the period, along with the royalist <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/monarchy-of-the-north">Monarchy of the North</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 28 May 1926 a military coup led by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-gomes-da-costa">Gomes da Costa</a> overthrew the republic and set up the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ditadura-nacional">Ditadura Nacional</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/first-portuguese-republic.jpg" alt="First Portuguese Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Columbano Bordalo Pinheiro Vector: Vítor Luís Rodrigues, António Martins-Tuválkin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Portugal_(official).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1910 CE – 1926 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lisbon</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Teófilo Braga, Afonso Costa, Sidónio Pais</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Portuguese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Portuguese First Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=first-portuguese-republic" aria-label="First Portuguese Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4453 789 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where First Portuguese Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4773 1045L4773 1045M4773 1045L4773 1044M4773 1045L4773 1045M4773 1045L4790 966"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4773 1045h0M4773 1044h0M4773 1045h0M4790 966h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4773 1045h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4773 1045h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Lisbon. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=first-portuguese-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
